# Suggested .gitignore additions when adopting the portable AI harness.
# Append these lines to your project's existing .gitignore if you want to keep
# the per-developer tool entry points and operational memory out of source
# control. Delete the lines you do want committed.
#
# Rationale:
# - `.ai/` is the canonical shared operational memory. Many teams choose to
#   commit `.ai/` so it travels with the project. Others keep it per-developer.
#   Decide per project; if you commit it, REMOVE the `.ai` line below.
# - Tool-specific entry points (`.claude/`, `.cursor/`, `AGENTS.md`,
#   `CLAUDE.md`, `opencode.json`) are usually per-developer because each
#   contributor may use a different tool. If your team standardizes on one tool
#   and wants the config committed, remove the matching lines.
# - `.opencode/` and `.codegraph/` directories are usually generated and should
#   stay ignored.

# >>> ai-harness >>>
.ai
.claude
.cursor
.opencode
.codegraph
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
opencode.json
# <<< ai-harness <<<
